  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Scattered rain showers and thunderstorms \ntonight through Tuesday, with some locally heavy rainfall \npossible. Surface smoke possible tonight.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nScattered showers will continue to build through the\nearly evening hours, mainly across the north. A front will cross\nthe area late tonight, bringing scattered rain showers and the\npossibility for a few thunderstorms. Any stronger showers and\nstorms could lead to locally heavier rainfall.\n\nThe progressive synoptic pattern has the potential to usher in\nwildfire smoke aloft, with brief ridges providing enough\nsubsidence that this smoke could push towards the surface,\nparticularly this evening prior to the next front which could\nclear the area out once more.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A round of widespread showers and thunderstorms\nexpected Thursday throughout much of the day. A strong storm or\ntwo is possible.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nA wave of upper level energy is expected to approach our area \nfrom the west Wednesday night and develop low pressure at the \nsurface which will move into our area Thursday bringing a round \nof widespread showers and thunderstorms. Some areas could see a \nsoaking rain based on where the strongest storms set up. Still \nuncertain right now as guidance is expressing some uncertainty \nin the position of the low pressure system but the North has the\ngreatest chance with the likelihood of at least 0.5\" of rain \naround 30%. Around 30-35 kts of deep-layer wind shear is \nexpected with at least several hundred J/kg of instability, \nalthough some models show 1000-1500 J/kg. Certainly something to\nwatch for rainfall potential and storm threat.",
